I agree.It's very hard to find out everything by yourself,even after
a long time of play.The experienced player still has the option 
to go wishless.
For example I don't allow myself to wish for items that I have
never encountered in the game (but only heard of somewhere).
Each player can make up his own mind how to handle this,and
that's a good thing.

If you don't know so much about the game it adds some kind of 
mysticism when you get a wish - there is a lot of black space you
wish to explore.The more you get,the more you can wish for 
next time. It's one thing that has always fascinated me about
Nethack and it would not work if the wishes were not 
granted _for sure_.

But as it's now, newbies get the chance to venture further into
the dungeon,gain more knowledge, and are likely to be 
fascinated about the game even more.

